<details class="analysis screen-only"><summary>{{ 'Course analysis guide' | t }} · {{ shortTitle | t }}</summary>
<p>{{ 'This is a course analysis diagram, not the artist’s historical process. Redraw by observation; use the guide to decide what to measure.' | t }}</p>
{% if number == 6 %}<div class="branch-diagram" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'Branch hierarchy: one trunk leads to three major limbs and then seven smaller limbs' | t }}"><div>{{ 'Trunk axis' | t }}</div><div>{{ 'Major limb 1 · Major limb 2 · Major limb 3' | t }}</div><div>{{ 'Smaller limbs → tapered twigs' | t }}</div></div><p>{{ 'Follow each branch from thick to thin. Change the fork angles and spacing; avoid a repeated pattern.' | t }}</p>
{% elif number == 3 or number == 7 or number == 9 %}<div class="value-guide" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'Three-value guide: light, middle, dark' | t }}"><span>{{ 'Light' | t }}</span><span>{{ 'Middle' | t }}</span><span>{{ 'Dark' | t }}</span></div><p>{{ 'Assign the largest shapes to these groups before choosing hatch marks. Paper can serve as the light.' | t }}</p>
{% else %}<div class="construction-guide {% if number >= 11 and number <= 14 %}head-guide{% elif number >= 17 %}figure-guide{% endif %}" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'Course construction guide' | t }}"><span class="guide-axis"></span><i class="anchor top"></i><i class="anchor left"></i><i class="anchor center"></i><i class="anchor right"></i><i class="anchor bottom"></i><span class="guide-mass one"></span><span class="guide-mass two"></span></div><p>{% if number == 10 %}{{ 'For an elevation, compare subdivisions across the centerline. For an oblique view, extend edges that are parallel in space toward a common vanishing point; separate different direction families.' | t }}{% elif number >= 11 and number <= 14 %}{{ 'Place the cranial envelope first. Tilt the face centerline and feature landmarks to match the observed head; these dots are measurement reminders, not universal facial proportions.' | t }}{% elif number >= 17 %}{{ 'Place rib cage and pelvis around the action line. Change their tilt and spacing to match the pose; use overlaps to connect the masses.' | t }}{% else %}{{ 'Choose your own highest, lowest, leftmost, and rightmost anchors. Adjust the central axis to the observed subject; check the envelope before refining the contour.' | t }}{% endif %}</p>{% endif %}
</details>
